 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## 2026-10-25 fixed diagonal-orientation lesson shortcut
+
+A source-pinned executable rival completes rectangle borders only for northwest-to-southeast equal-color corner pairs and ignores northeast-to-southwest pairs. At ordinary seed 252 all pairs in three demonstrations use the first orientation, so the rival fits them exactly; the query contains one opposite-diagonal pair and differs from the canonical output by eight cells. Both programs were replayed through protected Racket (8 evaluations total). The original lesson is therefore suitable for the optional alternative-answer stream, and production was not changed.
+
+Suggested lesson repair: show both diagonal orientations in the visible demonstrations, or add the fixed-orientation rival to admission. Evidence: `workspace/adversarial/diagonal-orientation-shortcut.json` and `checks/1713e09a3132/diagonal-orientation-shortcut.json`. This is a one-seed, one-rival finding.
