+
+## 2026-10-25 absolute-grid-half lesson shortcut
+
+A source-pinned executable rival classifies marker positions by the top/bottom and left/right halves of the whole canvas instead of relative to the cyan 2×2 block, while still writing into that block. At ordinary seed 0 it matches three generated demonstrations and differs on the fourth lawful query by two cells because a block-relative below-right marker remains in the top canvas half. Canonical and rival outputs were both replayed through protected Racket (8 evaluations total); the generator was not changed.
+
+Suggested lesson repair: require at least one visible example where block-relative quadrants disagree with whole-grid halves, or add this rival to lesson admission. Evidence: `workspace/adversarial/absolute-half-shortcut.json` and `checks/6143c7ef56be/absolute-half-shortcut.json`. This is a one-seed, one-rival finding, not universal ambiguity proof.
